## Conventions & Architectural Rules
- Use WidgetStateProperty (not MaterialStateProperty)
- Use CardThemeData (not CardTheme in ThemeData)
- Feature-based architecture with commons layer
- Keep existing comments and docstrings
- **Interface-First Architecture**: All Services and Repositories MUST have an abstract interface in `lib/interfaces/`
- **Dependency Inversion**: Higher layers (Cubits, Screens, Repos) must depend on Interfaces (e.g. `ILocationService`, `IAuthRepos`), not concrete implementations
- **Unit Test Mocks**: Mock services by `implements IService` to avoid constructor side-effects
- **Equatable Standard**: All BLoC/Cubit states must use `extends Equatable` (NEVER use deprecated `with EquatableMixin` or manual `operator ==`)
- **BLoC/Cubit Purity (Separation of Concerns)**:
  - NEVER hold or manipulate UI Controllers (`MapLibreMapController`, `ScrollController`, `TextEditingController`, `AnimationController`) inside Cubit/BLoC. Cubit is pure state & business logic.
  - UI Widgets hold controllers locally and react to Cubit state changes via `BlocListener` / `BlocConsumer`.
  - NEVER mix UI mixins (`with AppMixin`) or UI Context into Cubits, Services, or Repositories.
  - NEVER use `ValueNotifier` / `ChangeNotifier` controllers alongside Cubits for the same state (No Dual State Management).
  - Use Error Mapping Pattern instead of repetitive duplicate catch blocks in Cubit.
